---
title: Easy Homemade Bounty (Mounds) Bars
tags:
  - snack
  - treat
  - candy bar
  - chocolate
  - shredded coconut
  - sweetened condensed milk
servings: 12
time: 1 hour
---

In a medium #bowl, mix @unsweetened shredded coconut{255%g} and @sweetened condensed milk{300%g} to make a thick and sticky paste.

Using your hands, form some rectangles with the paste. Press firmly to make sure the rectangles will keep their shape. -- After 3 or 4 rectangles, wash your hands and do not dry them completely, so the paste won't stick to your hands.

Arrange the coconut bars on a #baking sheet{} lined with parchment paper and put in the freezer for ~{20%minutes}. -- This makes the candy easier to dip into chocolate. Don't skip this part or it'll be a mess!

In the meantime, cut @semisweet chocolate{425%g} into pieces and put two-thirds of it in a microwave-safe #bowl{}.

Microwave the chocolate on medium power for ~{30%seconds}, stir, then repeat in ~{15%seconds} intervals, until the chocolate has melted completely. [- Alternatively, melt on the stove top: place a heatproof bowl over a small saucepan filled with simmering water, and stir on low heat until melted, ensuring the chocolate doesn't touch the water or steam. -]

Add the remaining one-third of the chocolate and keep stirring until fully melted. -- This is called tempering: it gives the chocolate a glossy texture and a nice snap when set.

Remove the rectangles from the freezer. Using two forks, dip one rectangle halfway into the melted chocolate and roll it to coat all sides.

Using one fork, lift the rectangle out of the melted chocolate. With the other fork, scrape off excess chocolate, then arrange the bar on a lined baking sheet.

Allow a few hours for the chocolate coating to set -- time will vary depending on room temperature -- then enjoy your homemade bounty bars!

-- Storage: keeps up to 5 days in an airtight container, away from sunlight.
-- After that they'll start to dry out. Fridge storage dries and hardens them faster, so it's not recommended.
